From 36d2695d239e15f19d90ece139030a733ed8f0c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Strata layer <layer@studioz.local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:32:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] layer split: a batch slot's draft head keeps the main
 drafter's format (and a flag never ends the engine)

A slot's drafter does not build the draft head's token subset: it copies the main drafter's (dhead_, dvocab_,
n_dvocab_) and, until now, not its FORMAT.  dhead_type_ stayed at its -1 initial value, native_mmvq's dispatch
threw "unsupported native MMVQ GGML type" on the first draft of an admission, and the engine exited (exit 1): the
server then restarted the engine on every request that admitted a slot.  Found in a live run of this tree on
2026-10-07 (:5011, UD-IQ4_XS, --batch-mtp --layer-split auto --batch 4), first slot admission.

The type is now resolved by stage_plan.hpp's draft_head_type - the main drafter is the authority (the native head's
type, Q4_0 under --mtp-q4, or the Q6_K packed layout) - bind() refuses at start-up a draft head whose type has no
native MMVQ path (slot_mtp_reason), and no failure of this feature ends the process any more: a slot drafter that
cannot be built, a type that cannot run, or a draft that fails while serving turns --batch-mtp off with the reason
in the log and the slots go on decoding one token per window (the request is served).

This is upstream's omission - src/core/mtp.cpp is untouched by this layer, and v0.1.40.1 and main carry the same
missing copy in bind()'s `shared != nullptr` block - and it is NOT specific to a layer split: with an MTP rt that
carries draft_vocab.bin (the engine's own setup writes one, and the production rt here has one), upstream's
--batch-mtp fails the same way on ONE GPU.

tests/core/stage_plan_test.cpp pins the regression: a shared drafter takes the main one's type for each of the 17
native types and never resolves to -1.
